WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- [Matt] Hey, Legal Eagle.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.410
Where does skill end and chance begin

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:04.410
when it comes to gambling?

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.380
- Matt, I am so glad you asked

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.210
because every state has
different laws on this.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.560
Most states use what's called
the Dominant Factor Test.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.860
It determines whether
something is luck or skill.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.840
Is it about luck,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.610
or predominantly about skill?

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.870
And there are four subtests:

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.793
is the contest impossible
to win without skill?

00:00:19.793 --> 00:00:21.480
Does the average player have enough skill

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.570
to participate in the game?

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.560
Does skill determine the
actual result of the game,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.440
not simply an aspect of it?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.370
And are participants aware of the skill

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.650
and criteria that will be
used to determine the winner?

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.840
And I regret to inform you

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.440
that states are all over the map on this.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.730
Some states say that games
like Three-card Monte,

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.500
video games that award free replays,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.890
and puzzle games are games of skill.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.460
But generally, they agree
that games like Bingo or Dice

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.210
are completely about luck
and have no skill involved.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.480
And then when it comes to
games like Pinball and Poker,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.330
well, some states say
they're games of chance

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.520
and some say they're games of skill.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.670
So, it depends.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.300
But that's just a theory,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.553
a legal theory!

